# fortran-names.d/2026-11-05-step46-holidays -- the names of step 46's
# holidays (holidays.el, cal-julian.el, cal-islam.el, calendar.el).
#
# Decided by existing rules: predicates (_p) are is_* logical functions,
# but a function that returns two values is a subroutine named get_ plus
# what it returns (PORTING.md, R3-8): calendar-month-visible-p gives the
# visible year, calendar-nongregorian-date-visible-p the visible dates;
# no abbreviations (abs -> absolute).  calendar.el's variable
# calendar-mark-holidays is calendar_mark_holidays_variable (the clash
# rule's _variable suffix: the function calendar_mark_holidays has the
# name), by hand.  holiday-sexp is holiday_expression by the term entry
# sexp -> expression; its SEXP and the other Lisp forms of a holiday list
# are procedure pointers (R6-37).
